verview": "The Texas 23rd opened up when Rep. Tony Gonzales resigned in April, setting up a special contest between Republican gun-rights commentator Brandon Herrera and Democrat Katy Padilla Stout, with an independent also on the ballot. The district leans Republican by about seven points, and most expert raters place it as Likely or Lean Republican, though a couple see it as closer.\n\nHerrera has raised far more money than Stout, but he faces heavy outside opposition spending and unflattering coverage of past statements and an unfiled financial disclosure. National Democrats have added the seat to their target list. The balance of evidence points to a Republican hold with a modest margin, tempered by the nominee's vulnerabilities and limited fresh polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.355, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3283, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.203, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2999, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3496, "margin": -3.0}]}